A||||10||grizco||Passed A Cop at 100MPH
Z||000000||grizco||06-08-99||03:51 PM||||One day last week I was running late on my may to work so I was driving a little faster that usual. As I was aproaching the last intersection before I had to turn off the highway the light was still green so I floored it so I was sure to get through it before it changed. After going through the intersection I was going close to 110 mph. I looked across the highway and there was a State Trooper coming the other way. I though for sure that he had caught me withthe radar and I was going to get a ticket so i didn't bother to slow up any. After passing him I looked in my mirrors to see if he had his lights on and was turning around. You can imagine how lucky I felt when I looked in my mirrors and saw that he wasn't.
Z||000001||Patrick||06-08-99||04:19 PM||||<br>You went through an <b>intersection</b> at 110 mph?<p>Please don't bother to come down from Alaska to visit us here in British Columbia.<p>
Z||000002||grizco||06-08-99||05:37 PM||||Patrick-<br>At the time that I was going through the intersection I was only doing 85. When I passed the cop it was about a 1/4 mile down the road. The 110 was an estimated speed since the speedometer only goes up to 85, the needle was pointing straight down. I'm not even sure if my car will actually get to 110 since its an 84 SE with the iron duke four cylinder. If anybody knows the actual top speed of an 84 <br>SE I'd be interested in knowing what it is.
Z||000003||sluppy123||06-08-99||07:59 PM||||On a good day it might break 100.
Z||000004||Harry||06-12-99||04:12 PM||||I passed a Mass. state trooper doing 146mph one night, the only reason i didnt get slammed was (he knew me) and I dont really think he could have got up to speed in time to catch me before i got off the freeway.<br>(he called me on my cb radio and told me how fast i was going along with (*&^%%$#4)<br>UNFORTUNETLY this was not my Fiero!
Z||000005||Lynx||06-15-99||02:32 AM||||My Ferio is only a 85 SC with the four cylinder but it hauls ass. I dont know if ther has been any mods, but i can get the speedo all the way back to zero. Its WAY cool after you come back to zero the speedo just starts spinning in circles.
Z||000006||grizco||06-16-99||04:18 PM||||Harry- Where was the CB antenna mounted to get a good ground. I'm looking at adding one to my car. Also what did the car have in it for a motor.
Z||000007||Eric||06-16-99||08:58 PM||||Grizco,<br>It sounds like Harry didn't have a cb in his Fiero.  I do, however, have one in mine.  I grounded it under the bolt holding the passenger seat bracket.  It works for my dinky setup (Uniden cb and cellular look-alike glass mounted antenna).  I really only have it to listen to truckers.  It's almost as good as having a radar detector.
Z||000008||grizco||06-17-99||03:19 PM||||Thanks Eric I think I might look into adding an AM/FM/CB Combo antenna like what I have on my truck since it replaces the original antenna. It also gets better radio reception when its extended to its full length of 4 feet. If it won't fit right though I'll probably add the cellular look alike antenna.<br>Also where do you have your CB mounted. I was looking at mounting mine on the center hump.
Z||000009||Eric||06-17-99||07:37 PM||||I have my cb mounted on the bottom of the dashboard on the passenger side.  I really didn't want to go to the trouble of making a hole in the dashboard in order to mount it flush.  I don't use it too much, so I like having it someplace where I can remove it easily.  You can also run all the wires back into the center consol and splice the cig. lighter for power.  I have my antenna mounted right in the center of the rear window, so I can run the cable up through the glovebox and under the firewall insulation board.  You can hardly notice the whole thing.
Z||000010||Harry||06-18-99||10:11 AM||||Hey griz sorry Ive been at sea for the week!<br>No not my Fiero (im not really sure i want to go that fast in such a small car with no cage) this was a 77 camaro with a stroker motor. I was pushing around 400HP w\175HP NOS cheater plate. The tranny was a bullit proof T350 built for me by Bouchillon Performance out of Chas. SC.leading to a 3.73 posi unit.<br>The last one I built was a 72 Nova which was almost pro street ($ running low) which I eventually traded away for my 85 GT and 2K in cash.<br>After looking into what I got (went to the local library) and after a little research, lots of work and driving I fell in love with these little monsters!!!!!!<br>(theme song from Good bad and ugly playing in the back ground)
